"dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-19/omp-19/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/3/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/12.18.3 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/6e66a13a8fa112148a94c97b17706eed8dc1d73b/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` uses `int(amount * 100)`, which truncates float error (`19.99*100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 1998). Fix by converting through `Decimal` from the decimal string representation.\npytest isn't installed and couldn't be installed, so I'll run the tests directly.\nFixed. The bug was in `to_cents` in `ledger/currency.py`, not in `totals.py`.\n\n**Cause:** `to_cents` did `int(amount * 100)`. In floating point, `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999\u2026`, and `int()` cuts that down to `1998`. So any price whose binary form lands just below the true value lost a cent. That broke `test_subtotal_single` (19.99), `test_subtotal_qty` (0.29) and `test_total_discount` (4.35).\n\n**Fix** (`ledger/currency.py`): `to_cents` now converts the amount to a string first, then to a `Decimal`, multiplies by 100, and rounds half up to a whole cent. Converting via `str` uses the price as written (`\"19.99\"`) instead of its binary approximation. It also rounds properly instead of truncating, so cases like `0.1 + 0.2` correctly give `30`.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here and I couldn't install it, so I imported the test modules and called each test function directly. All four tests in `tests/test_totals.py` and `test_format` in `tests/test_report.py` passed. I also checked edge inputs: `-19.99 \u2192 -1999`, `10 \u2192 1000`, `1.005 \u2192 101`. The last one rounds up because rounding now follows the written decimal; the old code gave 100. To confirm with pytest, run `pytest tests/` once it's installed.\n\n**Remaining risk:** prices are still passed in as floats. The real fix is to have callers pass prices as `Decimal` or strings, or store them as integer cents. That would change the `Line` interface, so I didn't do it here.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 46046, "requests_cache_write": 32677, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2112422, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1930, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 4, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T03:24:36.985647+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 25.253, "t_checker_s": 0.429, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1942, "tokens_cache_read": 46046, "tokens_cache_write": 32677, "tokens_fresh": 1942, "tokens_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_cache_read": 46046, "tokens_main_cache_write": 32677, "tokens_main_calls": 5, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_output": 1930, "tokens_output": 1930, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 46046, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 32677, "tokens_proxy_calls": 5, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_proxy_o